# ABOUTME: Declares XSLoader's load and bootstrap_inherit: neither is ever exported.
# ABOUTME: Measured on perl 5.42.0 with XSLoader 0.32: neither sub carries a prototype.
package XSLoader;

# XSLoader exports nothing of its own -- measured on 5.42.0, it never
# calls Exporter and `use XSLoader;` installs no name, so `load()` called
# bare never resolves to XSLoader::load; even `use XSLoader qw(load);`
# installs nothing (measured: perl warns "Attempt to call undefined
# import method" and continues, not dying, with load still undefined in
# the caller). Every caller spells it out, `XSLoader::load(__PACKAGE__,
# $VERSION)`.
#
# Both subs end in a `goto` to a real extension's bootstrap function, or
# to DynaLoader's, so what they return depends on a compiled shared
# object the return-type oracle's call cases cannot safely supply --
# calling either with a name that resolves to a real extension would
# bootstrap it a second time, and one that does not resolve dies with
# "Can't locate loadable object", which is not evidence of the shape a
# real bootstrap returns. Each is declared Any and exempt.
sub load (List[Str] @args) Any;
sub bootstrap_inherit (List[Str] @args) Any;
